      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I am in total agreement with you. as a world builder myself, i'm finding it harder and harder to pack stuff into my world and srill keep it quest compatible. one thing that bugs me is that for some reason the quest side is larger than the pc side, even though every texture and mesh is exactly the same resolution or compressed for both sides. it's roughly a 10mb difference and that's a lot when it comes to the 100mb limit. 200 to 250 seems plenty resonable and if a world is optimised right with occlusion culling and render distances (among other optimizing techniques) then there should be no problem with the quest hardware. i've got plenty of questies that visit my world and have no problems.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-08-12T04:48:14.933Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "There is quite literally no reason as to why Quest has to have a hard limit on 100 MB to worlds, when I have seen Avatars over 100 MB on Quest that were fairly optimized and didn't cause any issues. I believe it should at least mbe increased to something like 200-250, because that would allow for way more content for Quest users, as the 100 MB limit can hold back Amazing worlds from being ported to Quest due to the file size not being able to be compressed to such a degree, and it would give Quest users more content, as I said before.",
